<protocol name="domain_awareness" type="routing" agent="pm">

## PURPOSE

Domain ownership matrix for PM routing decisions.
Defines WHO owns WHAT. For HOW to coordinate, load coordination_patterns.

---

## DOMAIN OWNERSHIP MATRIX

| Domain | Owns | Specialists/Analysts |
|--------|------|---------------------|
| **CATALOG** | Product data, families, variants, pricing, assets linking | catalog_analyst, catalog_specialist |
| **CREATIVE** | Image processing, asset creation, visual output, data-driven graphics | creative_specialist |
| **VISUAL** | Image analysis, visual identification, quality assessment | visual_analyst |
| **PRODUCT** | Product discovery, naming, positioning, market research | product_analyst |

---

## DOMAIN SCOPES

**CATALOG:** Product CRUD, families, variants, pricing, product-asset linking. Queries OUR database.

**CREATIVE:** Background processing, hero shots, lifestyle scenes, data-driven graphics, asset record creation (HITL for image quality)

**PRODUCT:** Product detective with access to all information on the internet. Naming, positioning, market keywords, how customers search. Returns comprehensive dossier.

**VISUAL:** Image analysis, identification, comparison (observation only, no editing)

---

## AGENT CAPABILITIES

### Visual Analyst
- **Role:** PM's EYES. Reports EVERYTHING visible.
- **Handles:** Comprehensive visual observation. Adapts focus by domain context.
- **Multi-image:** Determines relationship (same product/variants/different) when given multiple images.
- **Output:** visual_analysis_{image}.md - complete visual inventory + relationship pattern
- **Key:** Observations feed all downstream agents (creative, catalog, product).

### Catalog Analyst
- **Role:** Answers "What do WE have?" Database exploration.
- **Handles:** Any question about OUR catalog data. Family fit, pricing, duplicates.
- **Output:** catalog_analysis_{item}.md - findings relevant to the question
- **Key:** Recommendations are HYPOTHESES. Specialist verifies with real queries.

### Product Analyst
- **Role:** Answers "What IS this?" Outside world research.
- **Handles:** Naming, positioning, keywords, market research, how customers search.
- **Output:** product_research_{item}.md - comprehensive dossier enabling complete cataloging
- **Key:** Delegate the PRODUCT openly. Agent determines what to research.

### Creative Specialist
- **Role:** World-class commercial photographer. Creates visual assets.
- **Handles:** Material treatments, multi-item processing (individual/composite), quality iteration
- **Output:** Processed image + asset record (HITL for image quality). Returns asset_id.
- **Key:** Needs material info from visual analysis. Creates ASSET record, not product.

### Catalog Specialist
- **Role:** EXECUTION agent. Creates/modifies catalog with HITL.
- **Handles:** Product creation, variant structure, asset linking, schema discovery before writes
- **Output:** Product record + junctions. HITL shows business summary (SKU, name, price, family).
- **Key:** Receives ALL upstream files + asset_id. Links existing asset to product.

---

## ASSET OWNERSHIP (CRITICAL)

| Entity | Primary Owner | Can Also Create | HITL Concern |
|--------|---------------|-----------------|--------------|
| Asset record | creative_specialist | - | "Is this image acceptable?" |
| Product record | catalog_specialist | - | "Is this product data correct?" |
| product_assets junction | **Both** | Whoever runs second | Links asset to product |
| campaign_assets junction | creative_specialist | - | Links asset to campaign |

**Junction Rule:** Whoever runs SECOND creates the junction (they have the ID from step 1).
- Catalog first -> Creative creates product_assets (receives product_id)
- Images first -> Catalog creates product_assets (receives asset_id)

**Two-Stage HITL:** Creative handles image quality. Catalog handles product data. Separated concerns.

---

## ROUTING RULES (Gap-Based)

**Use Gap Analysis to determine who to call. See PM's `<delegation_doctrine>` for decision framework.**

### Single Image Requests

| User Request | Gaps to Fill | Route To |
|--------------|--------------|----------|
| Image + no text | **UNCLEAR** | Ask user: "What would you like me to do with this?" |
| Image + "add to catalog" | All (no context) | Visual -> Product -> Catalog |
| Image + family name | Visual details, IDs | Visual -> Catalog (skip Product) |
| Image + family + variant | Just IDs | Catalog only |
| Image + "what is this?" | Identity, Research | Visual -> Product |
| Image + "do we have this?" | Identity, Lookup | Visual -> Catalog |
| Image + "process/hero shot" | Material info (optional) | Visual (optional) -> Creative |

### Multiple Images - Determine Relationship FIRST

| User Signal | Relationship | Route To |
|-------------|--------------|----------|
| "this product" (singular) | Same product, angles | Visual (all) -> then gap-based |
| "parts" / "components" | Components of ONE product | Visual (all) -> then gap-based |
| "these sizes/colors" | Variants | Visual (all) -> then gap-based |
| "these products" (plural) | Different products | Visual (all) -> then gap-based per product |
| "compare" / "which one" | Comparison | Visual (all) -> Present to user |
| No text / unclear | **UNKNOWN** | Visual analyst determines relationship |

### Text-Only Requests

| User Request | Gaps | Route To |
|--------------|------|----------|
| "What IS this [name]?" | External research | product_analyst only |
| "Do WE have [X]?" | Internal lookup | catalog_analyst only |
| "Update/delete SKU-123" | None (direct action) | catalog_specialist only |
| "Add images to SKU-123" | None (product exists) | creative_specialist only |

### Gap-Based Routing Summary

| Gap Type | Who Fills It |
|----------|--------------|
| "Can't understand image" | visual_analyst |
| "Need external knowledge" | product_analyst |
| "Need internal data/IDs" | catalog_analyst |
| "Need image processing" | creative_specialist |
| "Need catalog writes" | catalog_specialist |

### When Multiple Analysts Needed

**IF you determine multiple analysts are needed (via gap analysis), sequence them:**

```
Visual -> Product -> Catalog
```

**Why this order (when all are needed):**
- Product analyst BENEFITS from visual findings (richer research)
- Catalog analyst BENEFITS from product research (better search context)

**But remember:** "Benefits from" =/= "Requires"
- Catalog CAN search with just family name (if user provided it)
- Product CAN research with just user description
- Only call analysts that FILL A GAP

**For coordination templates, load coordination_patterns.**

---

## DOMAIN BOUNDARIES

| Domain | IN Scope | OUT of Scope |
|--------|----------|--------------|
| CATALOG | Product CRUD, pricing, families, asset linking | External research, naming conventions |
| CREATIVE | Image processing, scene generation | Catalog records, pricing decisions |
| VISUAL | Image analysis, identification | Catalog queries, image editing |
| PRODUCT | Outside research, naming, positioning | Catalog data, image work |

---

## DOMAIN HANDOFFS

| From | To | Artifacts |
|------|-----|-----------|
| PM | ALL AGENTS | **Source image path** (when image-based workflow) |
| VISUAL | PRODUCT, CATALOG, CREATIVE, SPECIALIST | visual_analysis_{image}.md |
| PRODUCT | CATALOG, CREATIVE, SPECIALIST | product_research_{item}.md |
| CATALOG | CREATIVE, SPECIALIST | catalog_analysis_{item}.md |
| CREATIVE | CATALOG | asset_id (already HITL-approved) |

**CRITICAL: Source Image Goes to EVERY Agent**

All agents have multimodal capability. They can SEE images. Include source image path in EVERY delegation:

| Agent | Gets Source Image? | Why |
|-------|-------------------|-----|
| visual_analyst | YES | Primary analysis |
| product_analyst | YES | Can verify visual findings, see details |
| catalog_analyst | YES | Can compare with existing products visually |
| creative_specialist | YES | Source for processing |
| catalog_specialist | YES | Reference during record creation |

**WRONG:** Only passing images to visual_analyst
**CORRECT:** Every delegation includes `Source image at: inbox/photo.jpg`

**PM's role:** Route image paths, analysis files, and asset_ids between domains. Synthesize findings.

---

## DELEGATION PRINCIPLES

Every delegation MUST include:
1. **Source image path** - When image-based workflow (agents have multimodal capability)
2. **Domain context** - "For CATALOG domain"
3. **Upstream analysis files** - All relevant files from prior agents

**Note:** Company context is injected automatically by middleware - no need to include.

**For delegation templates and patterns, load coordination_patterns.**

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Anti-Pattern | Fix |
|--------------|-----|
| **Calling all analysts regardless of context** | Gap Analysis: only call analysts that FILL A GAP |
| **Parallel analyst calls** | When calling multiple: Sequential (V -> P -> C) |
| **Images only to visual_analyst** | Include source image in EVERY delegation |
| Missing domain context | Always specify "For X domain" |
| Cross-domain delegation | Creative creates images, Catalog links them |
| Skipping analysis when gaps exist | If you need the info, call the analyst |
| Calling analysts when user provided context | User authority: trust user-provided context |
| Missing file paths | Always include upstream analysis files (if they exist) |

</protocol>
